Z||000003||jelly2m8||11-21-2001||03:42 PM||||I assume you have at least the stock 215/60R15 tires on the rear of your 86 GT.<P> With the stock 215/60R14's the engine revs at 3000rpm +/- 50 rpm at 100kph/60mph<P> Also, which color VSS gear did you use?<p>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 11-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||The Aura||11-21-2001||04:04 PM||||The unit i got from the wrecker had the blue VSS gear... which was the one i ended up using. The one that came out of my car was a maroon color. The speedo seemed to be correct, but before i put the car away for the winter i noticed that the trip odometer was out a little bit...  could this be because of the "blue" gear or maybe an unrelated problem<P>------------------<BR>1986 GT 4spd&gt; Suspension Techniques Springs, Poly Bushings, Bosal Brospeed 4.5" Exhaust Tips||||reg||1
Z||000005||jelly2m8||11-21-2001||09:18 PM||||I couldn't remember which VSS gear I used when I had the 4.10 in my 87 GT. <P> Just did a few quick calculations, and the 195/70R14 tire comes in at less than 7/16" diference in height than the 215/60R15's. <BR> Basic rule of thumb is that a difference of 1/2" or less in height is acceptable without out any noticable effects on speedometer and ECM operation.<P> The P22 shows the red VSS gear to be used with the 4.10 / 195/70R14 combination.<P> Now that I think about it, that is what I used, the red gear.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Pontiaddict||11-21-2001||09:44 PM||||I'm pretty sure that the speedometer gear reads off of the final driven part of the transaxle, so the stock gear for the car would be the one you want to use. If you have the stock tires, you should use the red one. I'm pretty sure that when I changed the oil in my 4 speed 86gt, the gear was red. I'm pretty sure that the trans is stock.||||reg||1
